Description: Fix CVE-2026-44494 / GHSA-35jp-ww65-95wh prototype pollution gadget
 axios reads several sensitive configuration fields (proxy, socketPath,
 transport, lookup, beforeRedirect, httpAgent, httpsAgent) via plain property
 access in lib/adapters/http.js. Because these are not own properties of the
 default config object, lookup walks the prototype chain. An attacker who can
 pollute Object.prototype (via a separate prototype-pollution sink) can inject
 a malicious proxy entry, causing axios to silently route requests through an
 attacker-controlled proxy and leak credentials.
 .
 This is a minimal backport of the upstream fix (axios PR #10833 plus the
 follow-up commits 74a05bc and 17b90d0) tailored to v1.12.2:
   * lib/adapters/http.js: extend the own() helper (introduced by
     CVE-2026-42033's fix, applied earlier in the pipeline) to also guard
     httpAgent, httpsAgent, socketPath, proxy and beforeRedirect, so that
     polluted Object.prototype entries can no longer surface as request
     configuration.
   * lib/core/mergeConfig.js: no longer touched here — CVE-2026-42033's fix
     already reads config1/config2 via hasOwnProp for every merged prop, so
     that hardening is not duplicated in this patch.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/axios/axios/pull/10833
 also https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/74a05bc and
 https://github.com/axios/axios/commit/17b90d0
Bug: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-35jp-ww65-95wh
Author: Patch Platoon <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-08-10

