Backport of upstream axios PR #10858 (merge caa00a9, released as v1.16.1) to
axios v1.12.2, addressing AIKIDO-2026-10823 (CWE-319: HTTPS request data sent
in cleartext to HTTP proxy).

Root cause: setProxy() unconditionally rewrites options.hostname / port / path /
protocol to point at the proxy and switches the request into forward-proxy mode
for every proxied request, including https:// targets, so the proxy sees (and can
tamper with) the full URL, headers and body.

Fix: for HTTPS targets, install an inline CONNECT-tunnel https.Agent
(HttpsTunnelAgent, Node built-ins only - no new runtime dependency) on both
options.agent and options.agents.https, leaving hostname/port/path/protocol
pointing at the true origin so TLS SNI/verification apply to the origin.
Proxy-Authorization is sent only on the CONNECT request. User httpsAgent TLS
options are forwarded. HTTP targets keep the existing forward-proxy behavior.
On redirect, tunnel agents we installed are stripped (matched via a Symbol
marker) and the user's httpsAgent is restored. httpAdapter no longer clobbers
the tunnel agent when assigning options.agent.

